{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f52b000000000001","type":"group","x":-60,"y":0,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"01 · 预算授权与多年安排 | Budget authorisation","color":"5"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000002","type":"group","x":-60,"y":1400,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"02 · 统计范围与记录时点 | Coverage and timing","color":"5"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000003","type":"group","x":-60,"y":2800,"width":2370,"height":650,"label":"03 · 收入与举债融资 | Revenue and borrowing","color":"4"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000004","type":"group","x":-60,"y":3750,"width":2370,"height":650,"label":"04 · 统一账表与初级余额 | Fiscal balances","color":"4"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000005","type":"group","x":-60,"y":4700,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"05 · 债务存量与动态 | Debt stocks and dynamics","color":"6"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000006","type":"group","x":-60,"y":6100,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"06 · 跨期履约与风险 | Sustainability and risk","color":"6"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000007","type":"group","x":-60,"y":7500,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"07 · 资源、储蓄与代际 | Economic effects","color":"2"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000008","type":"group","x":-60,"y":8900,"width":2370,"height":650,"label":"08 · 到期资金与利率重置 | Refinancing and repricing","color":"2"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000009","type":"group","x":-60,"y":9850,"width":2370,"height":1100,"label":"09 · 周期调整与识别 | Cyclical adjustment","color":"3"},
		{"id":"f52b000000000010","type":"group","x":-60,"y":11250,"width":2370,"height":1650,"label":"10 · 规则、弹性与监督 | Rules and oversight","color":"3"},
		{"id":"f52e000000000001","type":"text","x":-60,"y":-400,"width":2370,"height":280,"text":"# 政府公债、预算制度与财政规则\n\n按编号自上而下阅读；区内箭头标明条件、核算或制度连接。颜色区分教学分区。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead the numbered sections from top to bottom. Arrows identify accounting links, conditions and institutional relationships; colours distinguish sections.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[02_Economy/02_public finance财政学/04_政府预算与公债融资|连续阅读：政府预算与公债融资]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000020","type":"text","x":0,"y":100,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 政府预算\n\n把政策、资金计划与相应授权连接起来。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Government budget*: policy, resources and authorisation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[政府预算|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000021","type":"text","x":600,"y":100,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 预算周期\n\n编制、批准、执行、报告与审计反馈。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Budget cycle*: preparation through audit and feedback.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[预算周期|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000023","type":"text","x":1200,"y":100,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 预算透明度\n\n让计划与执行信息及时、清楚且可比较。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Transparency*: timely, clear and comparable fiscal information.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[预算透明度|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000022","type":"text","x":0,"y":650,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 预算完整性\n\n全面呈现资金活动；不同活动可有不同授权程序。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Comprehensiveness*: full coverage with appropriate authorisation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[预算完整性|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000024","type":"text","x":600,"y":650,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 中期预算框架\n\n把多年成本与财政约束接入年度预算。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Medium-term framework*: connect future costs and limits to annual budgets.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[中期预算框架|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000025","type":"text","x":1200,"y":650,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 基线与上限\n\n基线预测现行政策成本；上限约束安排规模。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Baseline versus ceiling*: a cost projection versus a spending limit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[支出基线与支出上限|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000001","type":"text","x":1800,"y":100,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 从授权到执行\n\n初始预算、调整预算与决算先统一口径，再解释偏差；执行额不等于服务效果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReconcile original, revised and realised figures before explaining deviations. Spending outturn is not service effectiveness.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[预算支出与决算支出]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000004","type":"text","x":0,"y":1500,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 一般政府与公共部门\n\n控制与市场性质决定范围，名称不够。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Sector coverage*: control and market status determine the perimeter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[一般政府与公共部门|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000005","type":"text","x":600,"y":1500,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 财政合并口径\n\n抵销范围内对应交易与债权；不取消法律义务。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Consolidation*: eliminate internal claims, not legal obligations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政合并口径|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000006","type":"text","x":1200,"y":1500,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### 现金与权责发生\n\n分别看收付时点与经济事项发生时点。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Cash versus accrual*: payment timing versus economic recognition.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[现金与权责发生|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000017","type":"text","x":1200,"y":2050,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 财政拖欠\n\n款项已经到期仍未支付；未到期应付不算拖欠。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Arrears*: unpaid and overdue, not merely an unsettled payable.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政拖欠|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000001","type":"text","x":0,"y":2900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 政府公债\n\n举借取得资金，同时承担约定偿付义务。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Public borrowing*: funding in exchange for debt-service obligations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[政府公债|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000002","type":"text","x":600,"y":2900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 财政收入\n\nGFS 中，收入是交易带来的政府净值增加。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Revenue in GFS*: a transaction increases government net worth.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政收入|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000003","type":"text","x":1200,"y":2900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 收入与融资\n\n发债不是收入；金融与非金融资产出售分开记。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Revenue versus financing*: classify borrowing and asset sales precisely.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政收入与融资|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000002","type":"text","x":1800,"y":2900,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 从公债回到合同\n\n债券是债务证券，贷款也是举借方式。政府发行不消除违约风险；到期与息票依合同确定。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nBonds are debt securities; loans also finance borrowing. Government issuance does not eliminate default risk. Read contractual maturities and coupons.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债券]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000007","type":"text","x":0,"y":3850,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 财政赤字\n\n本卡 GFS 余额＝收入－费用－非金融资产净投资。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*GFS balance*: revenue minus expense and net nonfinancial investment.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政赤字|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000008","type":"text","x":600,"y":3850,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### 初级预算余额\n\n加回已说明口径的利息；初级盈余可与整体赤字并存。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Primary balance*: remove specified interest costs; an overall deficit can remain.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[初级预算余额|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000009","type":"text","x":0,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 总债务与净债务\n\n净债务只扣对应金融资产；不等于净值或可用现金。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Gross versus net debt*: eligible financial assets, not net worth or cash capacity.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[政府债务总额与净额|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000010","type":"text","x":600,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 存量流量调节\n\n赤字加金融资产、估值等调节，才解释债务变化。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Stock-flow adjustment*: reconcile deficits with debt changes.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债务存量流量调节|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000011","type":"text","x":1200,"y":4800,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 债务率动态\n\n同口径计算利差、初级余额和调节；保留增长分母。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Debt dynamics*: consistent interest, growth, primary balances and adjustments.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债务率动态|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000012","type":"text","x":1200,"y":5350,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 债务稳定初级余额\n\n令债务率变化为零，算所需盈余；可行性另检验。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Stabilising balance*: set the ratio change to zero; test feasibility separately.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债务稳定初级余额|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000013","type":"text","x":0,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 政府跨期预算约束\n\n债务对应未来盈余与终端债务现值；终端项需条件才能消去。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Intertemporal budget*: surplus and terminal-debt present values, with explicit limits.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[政府跨期预算约束|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000015","type":"text","x":600,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 债务可持续性\n\n联合检查可行财政路径、融资条件与冲击。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Sustainability*: feasible fiscal paths, financing and shocks jointly.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债务可持续性|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000014","type":"text","x":1200,"y":6200,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### 财政或有负债\n\n特定未来事件触发支付；暴露额不等于预期损失。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Contingent liabilities*: triggered payments; exposure is not expected loss.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政或有负债|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000016","type":"text","x":600,"y":6750,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 利差的判断边界\n\n利率低于增长只改善利差项，不保证可持续。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Interest-growth limits*: a favourable differential is not a sustainability guarantee.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[利差与债务可持续性|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000003","type":"text","x":1800,"y":6200,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 先折现，再加总\n\n跨期比较先统一日期和贴现因子；有限期账户仍保留终端资产或债务。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nUse one valuation date and appropriate discount factors. A finite account retains terminal assets or debt.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[现金流同点折现加总]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000004","type":"text","x":1800,"y":6750,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 救助预期与事前激励\n\n可预期的事后救助可能软化借债约束；常规转移本身不足以判断。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nExpected ex-post support can soften borrowing constraints. Ordinary transfers alone do not establish the mechanism.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[软预算约束]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000040","type":"text","x":0,"y":7600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 融资与资源成本\n\n固定购买路径时，举债不推迟已发生的资源占用。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Funding versus resources*: debt does not postpone today's given purchase.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[公债融资与资源成本|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000041","type":"text","x":600,"y":7600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 公债挤出条件\n\n固定购买与收入，检查私人储蓄抵消及经济开放性。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Crowding out*: fixed purchases and income; saving offsets and openness matter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[公债挤出条件|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000042","type":"text","x":1200,"y":7600,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 公债代际负担\n\n同一基准下核算税款、债权收益与承接的真实资产。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Generational incidence*: taxes, creditor receipts and real assets against one baseline.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[公债代际负担|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000043","type":"text","x":0,"y":8150,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 李嘉图等价\n\n固定购买与偏好，完整可行集合相同，税收时点不改变消费选择。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Ricardian equivalence*: fixed purchases, preferences and the complete feasible set preserve consumption choices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[李嘉图等价|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000044","type":"text","x":600,"y":8150,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 借贷约束与税收时点\n\n借贷上限确实绑定时，延期税可放松当期消费限制。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Binding credit limits*: tax deferral can relax current consumption constraints.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[借贷约束与税收时点|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000045","type":"text","x":1200,"y":8150,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 代际联系与债务中性\n\n未来税负需进入当前可调整计划；有限寿命本身不够判定。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Family links*: future taxes must enter an adjustable plan; finite life alone is insufficient.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[代际联系与债务中性|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000005","type":"text","x":1800,"y":7600,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 核算之后还要行为\n\n储蓄恒等式不决定消费、产出或利率反应。需求效果取决于闲置资源、政策构成与融资环境。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSaving identities do not determine consumption, output or interest responses. Slack, policy composition and financing conditions matter.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政政策]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000046","type":"text","x":0,"y":9000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 公债再融资风险\n\n到期续借可能异常昂贵，也可能无法取得资金。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Refinancing risk*: unusually costly or unavailable replacement funding.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[公债再融资风险|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000047","type":"text","x":600,"y":9000,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### 再融资与利率重定价\n\n本金到期与息票重置分开；长期浮息债仍可重定价。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Rollover versus repricing*: long maturity need not fix interest costs.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[再融资与利率重定价|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000028","type":"text","x":0,"y":9950,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 财政自动稳定器\n\n既有税收与给付规则随经济状态变化，缓冲收入波动。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Automatic stabilisers*: existing tax and benefit rules cushion income fluctuations.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政自动稳定器|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000029","type":"text","x":600,"y":9950,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 周期调整预算余额\n\n按产出缺口和收支弹性，扣除估计的周期成分。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*CAB*: remove estimated cyclical effects using output and fiscal elasticities.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[周期调整预算余额|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000030","type":"text","x":1200,"y":9950,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 结构性预算余额\n\n周期调整后，再列明一次性及其他暂时性调整。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Structural balance*: explicitly extend cyclical adjustment for temporary factors.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[结构性预算余额|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000031","type":"text","x":1200,"y":10500,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 结构性余额的识别边界\n\n估计修订不是新增政策；余额变化不直接识别因果效果。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Interpretation limits*: revisions are not new measures or causal effects.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[结构性余额的识别边界|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000006","type":"text","x":1800,"y":9950,"width":430,"height":350,"text":"### 周期基准是估计\n\n潜在产出不是已知物理上限；产出缺口取决于基准与数据版本，比较时固定口径。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPotential output is estimated, not a known physical maximum. Output gaps depend on the benchmark and data vintage.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[潜在产出]] · [[产出缺口]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000026","type":"text","x":0,"y":11350,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 财政规则\n\n对财政总量施加持续性数值约束。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Fiscal rule*: a lasting numerical constraint on fiscal aggregates.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政规则|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000027","type":"text","x":600,"y":11350,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 债务锚与操作规则\n\n长期债务参照通过余额或支出约束连接年度选择。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Anchor and operation*: connect long-term debt aims to annual choices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[债务锚与操作规则|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000032","type":"text","x":1200,"y":11350,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 预算余额规则\n\n先说明总体、初级或调整余额，再检验赤字界限。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Balance rule*: specify the aggregate before testing a deficit limit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[预算余额规则|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000033","type":"text","x":0,"y":11900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 支出规则\n\n约束支出水平或增速；范围与分母影响周期弹性。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Expenditure rule*: scope and denominators shape cyclical flexibility.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[支出规则|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000034","type":"text","x":600,"y":11900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"1","text":"### 余额规则与顺周期\n\n年度观测余额约束可能迫使衰退紧缩；固定 CAB 不自动容许额外刺激。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Procyclicality*: annual limits may force tightening; fixed CAB limits need not allow extra stimulus.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[余额规则与顺周期|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000035","type":"text","x":1200,"y":11900,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 财政逃逸条款\n\n异常冲击下授权暂时偏离，并明确监督与回归。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Escape clause*: authorised temporary deviation with oversight and return.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政逃逸条款|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000036","type":"text","x":0,"y":12450,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 独立财政机构\n\n依授权提供专业非党派分析，不代替预算决策。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Independent fiscal institution*: mandated analysis, not a replacement for budget decisions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[独立财政机构|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000037","type":"text","x":600,"y":12450,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 财政规则覆盖边界\n\n固定机构、交易、基础与例外，才知道规则约束什么。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Rule coverage*: identify institutions, transactions, accounting and exceptions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政规则覆盖边界|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52a000000000038","type":"text","x":1200,"y":12450,"width":350,"height":350,"color":"3","text":"### 财政规则合规与效果\n\n有规则、实际遵守和经济效果，需要不同证据。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Adoption, compliance and effects*: three separate evidential questions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政规则合规与效果|打开原子]]"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000007","type":"text","x":1200,"y":3850,"width":1030,"height":350,"text":"### 从账表到债务\n\n赤字加金融资产净取得、估值等[[债务存量流量调节|存量流量调节]]，解释同口径债务存量的变化；各期存量再除以各期 GDP，得到[[债务率动态|债务率的变化]]。赤字不能直接当作债务增量，也不能直接当作债务率增量。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nReconcile the deficit with net financial-asset acquisition, valuation and other stock-flow adjustments to explain debt-stock changes on a consistent basis. Divide each period's stock by its GDP to obtain debt-ratio dynamics. The deficit alone does not identify either change.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000008","type":"text","x":1200,"y":9000,"width":1030,"height":350,"text":"### 从到期资金到可持续性\n\n到期能否续接，是[[债务可持续性]]中的融资条件之一。到期再融资与息票重置，使市场利率变化逐步影响存量平均利率；[[债务率动态]]中的有效利率不能直接替换为当天新债收益率。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRollover access is one financing condition within debt sustainability. Market-rate changes affect the average cost of outstanding debt through refinancing and coupon resets; today's new-bond yield is not automatically the effective rate in debt dynamics.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"f52c000000000009","type":"text","x":1800,"y":11350,"width":430,"height":900,"text":"### 长期约束怎样进入年度规则\n\n[[债务率动态]]与[[债务稳定初级余额]]提供条件化核算，支持[[债务锚与操作规则]]的校准；[[债务可持续性|可行性与风险]]仍须另检验。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDebt dynamics and stabilising balances inform rule calibration conditionally. Feasibility and risks still need separate tests.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[周期调整预算余额|周期调整]]与[[结构性预算余额|结构调整]]决定用什么余额检验[[预算余额规则]]；先固定估计口径，再谈遵守。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCyclical and structural adjustments define the balance tested by a rule. Fix the estimation basis before assessing compliance.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n[[财政逃逸条款]]为重大冲击提供授权偏离、监督和回归程序。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEscape clauses govern authorised deviation, oversight and return after major shocks.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
